<!--
  Build-only placeholder. Every value is obviously fake and grants nothing.

  `lib/main.dart` calls `Firebase.initializeApp()`, which throws at startup on
  iOS when `ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist` is absent. The real file is
  gitignored, correctly, so a fresh clone has nothing to load. Copy this into
  place to get the app booting:

      cp test/e2e/GoogleService-Info.placeholder.plist ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist

  With these values Firebase initialises but every Firebase-backed feature —
  push notifications and crash reporting — is inert. For anything real, create
  your own Firebase project and download the genuine file. See the README.
-->
